{"availability":"available","full":"TimvdLippe/internship-report-google","name":"internship-report-google","description":"The report about my internship at Google on the Polymer team","category":"Other","language":null,"stars":89,"forks":4,"created":"2017-10-10T11:30:06Z","updated":"2017-12-19T20:59:22Z","branch":"master","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://ebidel.github.io/material-playground/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T14:33:18.945Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-03T14:33:18.945Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-03T14:33:18.945Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T14:33:18.945Z","stars":89,"forks":4}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["In the summer of 2017, I did an internship at the Polymer team in the San Francisco office of Google. This internship included training by top engineers about the inner-workings of Google as a company, how to use the tooling for the daily developer workflow as well as a real-world project. The real-world project concerned the load time of large web applications, focused on one of the biggest users of Polymer: Youtube.","This report contains an overall impression of the working environment at Google in comparison to my university, a description of the full internship, the technical aspects of the task that was given as well as an insight in the way Google can do software engineering on a large scale.","Aside from obtaining experience from working at Google, the most important part of the internship was the real-world project. Load time of applications is of great concern for Youtube as well as various other big users of Polymer. As such, Youtube requested the Polymer team for improvements to their load performance. Earlier examples of improved load performance was the introduction of lazyRegister. lazyRegister specifically aimed to reduce the amount of registration and setup work Polymer did when registering elements. As Youtube is a big application, it builds and uses a lot of custom…"],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/TimvdLippe/internship-report-google/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"93c7ccb15c6aa930b7237050296374ccd69287e790d78869a95203090de6bbc1","extractedAt":"2026-10-03T06:27:07.350Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T10:48:19.860Z","overviewRepoUpdated":"2017-12-19T20:59:22Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T10:48:19.867Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"In the summer of 2017, I did an internship at the Polymer team in the San Francisco office of Google. This internship included training by top engineers about the inner-workings of Google as a company, how to use the tooling for the daily developer workflow as well as a real-world project. The real-world project concerned the load time of large web applications, focused on one of the biggest users of Polymer: Youtube.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/TimvdLippe/internship-report-google/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"93c7ccb15c6aa930b7237050296374ccd69287e790d78869a95203090de6bbc1","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/TimvdLippe/internship-report-google/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-03T10:48:19.861Z"},"readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/TimvdLippe/internship-report-google/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-03T10:48:19.863Z","hash":"93c7ccb15c6aa930b7237050296374ccd69287e790d78869a95203090de6bbc1","originalBytes":45647,"storedBytes":45647,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["polymer","metadata","property","element","custom","time","tool","bindings","such","binding","performance","properties","able","example","were","load","results","template","used","which","google","working","browser","mobile","node","required","there","after","content","internship","parsing","tests","well","work","core","figure","only","data","definition","effects","project","several","team","back","build","code","desktop","first","however","instead","thus","user","very",